From 5a5b04c09a80984c6a27fc3ef4fe5231812faac9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 02:09:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/25] Cross-check RV-Pratishakhya uncertain readings against
 VedaVishtaram

Adds tools/pratishakhya/crosscheck_vedavishtaram.py: attaches
VedaVishtaram's sutra text + Uvata's Bhasya to 1,007 of 1,067 items,
hand-resolves 24 of patala 10-11's 26 has_uncertain_reading sutras
(each with a citation of exactly how -- direct match or a named
corpus-internal pattern, never a guess; 2 left deliberately unresolved),
and resolves 85 more elsewhere in the corpus via unambiguous automated
matching (135 remain unresolved, down from 258).

Two real bugs caught and fixed along the way, not silently avoided:
Sanskrit Library's SLP1 uses "x" for the Vedic retroflex lateral la,
not standard SLP1's vocalic l -- this had been mis-transliterating 35
sutras since the very first import (confirmed via VedaVishtaram's own
Bhasya naming the grammarian vyALi in plain Devanagari). And the
automated resolver had a real matching bug where an uncertain
character at a word's edge let an unanchored regex swallow the wrong
span, caught concretely on sutra 1.39 coming back with a visibly
duplicated phrase -- fixed and guarded by a regression test.

